# MOVEMENT I — DEVELOPMENT part b: climax (b131-146) and retransition
# (b147-160).
# b131-138: the CELL in ALL strings (vn at +16, va +8, vc, cb -8; fg) on
#   Ab, Bb, Cm, D (two bars each, bass rising ab-bb-c-d) while fl+ob
#   proclaim the T1 head in augmentation (4th up + steps) each time a step
#   higher, landing on the b9 E-flat over D (b138).
# b139-146: D pedal, L5; eb-d sighs; Ger6 (eb g bb c#); unison D arpeggio.
# b147-160: the long fade: L3 -> L2 -> L1 -> vc ALONE pp (b153-156, the
#   quietest moment of the movement) with ghostly T1 head in fl/ob,
#   then a four-bar crescendo to the recapitulation.

